note over COLLECTOR,DOCKER
  The selected builder reports configured limits,
  not proof that its workers enforce those caps.
  Ordinary build flags do not establish actual
  resource bounds, so a metadata pass retains
  the enforcement question.
end note

note over DOCKER
  The Engine cache and selected builder can
  store the same image in different places.
  A cached image record therefore cannot prove
  offline build support or the copied
  interpreter's startup compatibility.
end note

  COLLECTOR -> FILES : exclusive receipt <=64 KiB or fail\nPASS_METADATA_ONLY / FAIL_METADATA_ONLY, explicit unknowns
  COLLECTOR --> FISH : metadata-only status; no retry or build authority\nquery-owned process-group TERM/KILL timers, not physical-stop proof
  FISH -> FILES : post-exit worker diagnostic check <=64 KiB/stream SOFT ONLY\ncommand.exit + HOST_BUILD_INVENTORY_EXIT after syntax failure too
  FISH --> EXECUTOR : FUTURE actual HOST output including HOST_BUILD_INVENTORY_EXIT\nreceipt if created, first failure STOP/retain partial outputs/zero retries

note over COLLECTOR,FILES
  Overflow retains each stream's original prefix,
  rather than trimming evidence into success.
  The parent checks diagnostics only after exit,
  so its soft size check cannot establish
  a streaming quota.
end note

